# the looper builds the road: a take into part A (AUTO), then into B (the tape's K2 PART) - each a block by itself;
# on ROAD HOME + K1 moves a block, COPY + PASTE copy a block's notes into another, CLONE makes a new part from one;
# REC on ROAD records like anywhere; the tape's ALGO is the count-in (4 clicks)
wait 300
tap SAVE
wait 100
tapkey w4
wait 200
expect nroad 1
press HOME
tapkey b0
release HOME
tap REC
wait 3200
key w4 down 100
wait 400
key w4 up
wait 5900
tap REC
wait 200
expect bars 2
expect nroad 1
expect road0 0
tap PLAY
wait 100
turn K2 1
wait 50
expect part 1
turn ALGO -1
turn ALGO 1
wait 50
expect counting 0
tap REC
wait 300
expect counting >0
wait 3000
key w6 down 100
wait 400
key w6 up
wait 3000
tap REC
wait 200
tap PLAY
wait 100
expect nroad 2
expect road1 1
shot blocks_tape.png
# ROAD: the second block moved to the front
tap ENV
wait 50
turn K1 1
wait 50
expect roadpart 1
press HOME
turn K1 -1
release HOME
wait 50
expect road0 1
expect road1 0
# COPY block 1 (part A), PASTE into block 0 (part B): B's piano notes become A's
turn K1 1
tapkey b9
turn K1 -1
mark
tapkey b10
wait 50
expect eventsB1 >0
# CLONE: a new part (C) after it, the notes copied
tapkey b8
wait 50
expect nroad 3
expect road1 2
expect eventsC1 >0
press EDIT
wait 800
release EDIT
wait 50
expect nroad 2
shot blocks_road.png
# REC on ROAD: a recording, not the old road recording
tap REC
wait 200
expect counting >0
tap REC
expect textfit 0
